From 043cb0b8c01b5ecb114afb10462b4a57bffb0efe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Singh <nathan.singh@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:03:31 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Arena: the attendant warns when the next round is a boss or a
 mini-boss

cupdata.py: R(..., boss=0/1/2); left out it is derived (finish_bosses): the last
round of a main cup, or of a side cup with a story boss, and every Boss Rush
round are bosses (2); any other round with a story boss is a mini-boss (1).
gen-cups.py writes them as two bitmasks in ArenaCupInfo (miniBossRounds in the
old pad, bossRounds in pad2; same size). After "Round n won!" the attendant
shows one more message, MsgArenaBossWarning ("Watch out! The next round is a
boss!") or MsgArenaMiniBossWarning ("Careful! A tough opponent is next!"), when
round n + 1 is marked. Round 1 never has one. New messages above the generated
block; gen-cups.py re-run (ids moved by two).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
